# Ignore the two places a real secret ends up once you run this
# Terraform: the tfvars file you copied from terraform.tfvars.example and
# filled in with a real db_password, and every Terraform state file.
#
# State matters as much as tfvars, not less: Terraform writes db_password
# into terraform.tfstate IN PLAINTEXT so it can detect drift on the next
# plan/apply. An ignored terraform.tfvars sitting next to a committed
# terraform.tfstate still leaks the same password -- ignoring only the
# file you typed the secret into and not the file Terraform copied it
# into is not a fix, it only moves which file leaks it.
terraform.tfvars
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
.terraform/
